Possibly a spoiler concerning named weapons/cheating.  Read at your own
discretion.















	I've been playing Nethack on PL 6 with a Barbarian character.  I found
an altar to Morrigan on level 5, and began hanging around, killing
things and feeding them to my diety.  A few four-leafed clovers later, i
found a named weapon at my feet--the orcish dagger named Grimtooth
(drat!  hoping for Stormbringer!).
	I grumbled a little, and proceeded to test the karma of my new weapon
(blessed/uncursed/cursed).  I dropped it on the altar and picked  it up.
 Suddenly, instead of a halbard, Grimtooth, and 3 uncursed orcish
daggers i had a halberd and "4 uncursed orcish daggers named Grimtooth".
Being the enterprising sort, i decided to test this further, and picked
up some more daggers, and ended up with 13 Grimtooths (you get a lot of
weapons when you hang around to kill things).  I suppose similar weapons
(same plus, karma) are grouped without regard to name in your inventory.
	This story has a sad ending because i tried to convert some other
uncursed daggers via the altar.  Two of them stayed separate, but the
third was grouped with the others--and i got "14 uncursed orcish
daggers".  Either the grouping works both ways, or the gods were just
fed up with my being greedy.  I don't think i'll try for another named
weapon, since the dwarves and rock moles really messed up level 5, and
anyway i'd probably just get Grimtooth again.  
	Admittedly there really isn't much use for 13 Grimtooths (maybe they're
worth a little more gold than regular Orcish daggers, but not much). 
But i shudder to think what 6 or 7 Mjollnirs or Stormbringers could do
for a character.  I'm pretty sure this wasn't an intentional fixture of
Nethack, but a loophole in the rules.  It might have been fixed in PL 7
or PL 8. 

Just my .02 zorkmids.  Oh, btw, i'm, sorry for posting that rumor about
dragon scale/scroll of fire.  Either way, don't genocide dragons--wipe
out water moccasins!  Make fountains a safer place.

